title: ActivityLog builds invalid ref names from ordinary email addresses
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

`ActivityLog.pm:58` sanitises the git email into a ref name but leaves `.`
untouched, so `a..b@example.com` produces an invalid ref and the command dies
**after** it has already written:

    git config user.email 'a..b@example.com'
    karr pick --claim x
      -> libgit2 error -12 (klass 4): the given reference name
         'refs/karr/log/user/a..b_example.com' is not valid      rc=1
    git show refs/karr/tasks/1/data:data -> claimed_by: x    # claim written anyway
    git for-each-ref | grep lock -> refs/karr/tasks/1/lock   # lock left behind

Same for an address containing `.lock`. `KARR_ROLE` goes through the same
sanitiser, so a role name can trigger it too.

Two things to fix: sanitise against the actual git ref-name rules (no `..`, no
trailing `.lock`, no leading/trailing `.`), and validate the ref name *before*
doing any writing so a bad name cannot leave a half-applied command behind.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
